{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition","id":1523395,"title":"Five Atlanthean Mysteries and Egregore in Second Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-01T01:08:39-07:00","id":1523395,"title":"Five Atlanthean Mysteries and Egregore in Second Edition","content":"In first edition, as I understand it, Status in the Mysterium and experiencing Mysteries were tied to each other. You could not climb the ranks without experiencing Mystery of corresponding level; experiencing the Mystery bestowed upon you the benefits of increased status amongst mystagogues. But in the second edition, Egregore is now a style requiring only first dot of Mysterium Status; it can be increased without Gnosis or Arcana requirements. Theoretically, starting character with 5 dots in Egregore is possible. While I fully support that from mechanical point of view, this creates a gap between mechanics and fluff (of first edition), where very young mage experienced and won Mysteries which are far out of his reach, yet. How one could reconcile old fluff and current mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T01:42:22-07:00","id":1523397,"title":"","content":"Simple; either that Status 1 Mage fell from grace (and used to have a lot more Status, good if the Mage has a bunch of experience) or someone failed to sufficiently gatekeep the knowledge of Egregore and the Mage in question learned it above their level illicitly.<br /> Either way, story hook.<br /> <br /> In the later case, I would discuss with the Player/GM what the consequences of getting caught with it above their paygrade would be. A death sentence is a lot to spring on someone, but indentured servitude is not pleasant either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T01:59:40-07:00","id":1523398,"title":"","content":"I think it's better to draw inspiration from the original version to lean in to the distinct tracks, rather than try to retain it directly. Have an idea that the Mysterium (at least in its modern form) has some delineation between the status that bestows rank of prestige and responsibility in caucus and the larger network, and level of immersion in and dedication to the mystery.<br /> <br /> Outside of player characters I'd say it's still uncommon to have mages of lower rank have the capacity for higher initiation (or fellows willing to induct them), but not impossible in the event that somebody fundamentally gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T07:17:51-07:00","id":1523408,"title":"","content":"I think what Dark Archon means is how do you reconcile the fluff of there being a certain amount of exclusivity with the fact that everyone and their mother can start with maxed Egregore (as long as they are Mysterium)?<br /> <br /> The answer is that they can't. Every single Merit implies some backgroud or other aspect of your character. If you can't motivate the purchase of a Merit, you just don't buy it. That's the same reason why not everyone can start with Resources 5 (the level described as &quot;filthy rich&quot;) even though there's technically no prerequisites whatsoever for the Resources Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T07:36:49-07:00","id":1523409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition?p=1523408#post1523408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what Dark Archon means is how do you reconcile the fluff of there being a certain amount of exclusivity with the fact that everyone and their mother can start with maxed Egregore (as long as they are Mysterium)?<br /> <br /> The answer is that they can't. Every single Merit implies some backgroud or other aspect of your character. If you can't motivate the purchase of a Merit, you just don't buy it. That's the same reason why not everyone can start with Resources 5 (the level described as &quot;filthy rich&quot;) even though there's technically no prerequisites whatsoever for the Resources Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so bad if everybody in a small group of people wanted to start with Resources 5, even if they weren't putting a lot of thought into the backstory of it.<br /> <br /> If it actually is a question of &quot;it's easier to have a thing at character creation than it would be to acquire it in narrative terms&quot;, that's easily answered with the reminder that character creation is an abstraction for the benefit of flexibility for the sort of character one wishes to begin with, that includes some necessary opportunity costs; starting with anything at five dots imposes a lot of limits on any other Merits one might want to have.<br /> <br /> These are game mechanics that primarily exist for the purpose of playing the game rather than being representations of the relative value of and difficulty in attaining a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T07:41:06-07:00","id":1523411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition#post1523395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In first edition, as I understand it, Status in the Mysterium and experiencing Mysteries were tied to each other. You could not climb the ranks without experiencing Mystery of corresponding level; experiencing the Mystery bestowed upon you the benefits of increased status amongst mystagogues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to fill this in a bit, every mystagogue was supposed to undergo the ritual that would provide them with deeper insight into their mystical beliefs at each level of rank initiation, but not all of them would then get the Atlantean Mystery benefits. One had to buy that as a separate Merit anyway, to represent it having the most profound resonance that allowed them to actively tap into the egregore, as opposed to having it as an abstract idea of the connection between Mysterium members and experienced reality of living magic.<br /> <br /> That's part of why I think it's possible to put a bit of a wedge in there to widen a bit into more separate tracks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T09:22:10-07:00","id":1523426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition?p=1523409#post1523409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's so bad if everybody in a small group of people wanted to start with Resources 5, even if they weren't putting a lot of thought into the backstory of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much &quot;you need to fully explain how this fits your character&quot; as it's just making sure the character is consistent. If your character is established as a newly inducted Mysterium member, it wouldn't be consistent to have gone through multiple initiations into deeper circles of the order, just like it wouldn't make sense for my established struggling artist on the verge of homelessness to suddenly have Resources 5 just because I happened to have the XP required to buy five Merit dots.<br /> <br /> But if you can explain it, just go for it as long as you're not breaking the tone of the game. Sometimes you could even buy Merits that retroactively adds background information that previously wasn't relevant. &quot;My character has always been filthy rich. He just prefers not to bring attention to it, and we've just never had a reason to spend money before.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T18:00:35-07:00","id":1523446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition?p=1523426#post1523426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your character is established as a newly inducted Mysterium member, it wouldn't be consistent to have gone through multiple initiations into deeper circles of the order</div> </div> </div> </div>Basic character creation refers to somebody Awakened somewhere between several months and a year. If they have a particular proclivity for it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">just like it wouldn't make sense for my established struggling artist on the verge of homelessness to suddenly have Resources 5 just because I happened to have the XP required to buy five Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Batman Begins.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T04:57:57-07:00","id":1523539,"title":"","content":"There is nothing stopping a deeply committed member of the mysterium from retaining status 1 after years if they don't take on any status related work/roles, right?<br /> <br /> But i think mechanically the bigger issue is that a guardian or ladder member can take mysterium status 1 and thus would have earned the pre-req for taking the eregore merit.<br /> <br /> Which i think the fluff does not support at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T06:33:03-07:00","id":1523548,"title":"","content":"You know, RPGs often have something called the golden rule: &quot;if you don't like something, change it&quot;.<br /> <br /> The game Exalted has an additional one they called the orichalcum rule: &quot;we can't anticipate absolutely every confluence of the rules, and if you figure out one that seems particularly broken or not fun or contrary to the setting or themes, probably best to disregard it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T09:09:17-07:00","id":1523556,"title":"","content":"There's also always the divide between &quot;I've met the mechanical pre-requisite&quot; and &quot;In game, no-one is willing to teach me&quot;. The second must be used carefully by an ST, balancing what makes a good story, because blanket stonewalling can be just as un-fun to play with. Maybe there's a heretical Heirophant out there who will initiate members of other Orders who've achieved Mysterium Status 1, but requires a major task before he'll do so. Suddenly this turns into a sub-plot, rather than someone getting a bit Munchkin-y.<br /> <br /> (That being said, I <i>do</i> think the Silver Ladder teaches the Lex Magica Merit to others much more readily that the Mysterium would hand out Egregore. It's useful to Sentinels and other Consillium officials, and those are the most likely to have some tie to the Ladder &quot;Look! Participating in the system we set up makes you better at magic! <i>Participate in our system, damn you</i>!&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T13:08:24-07:00","id":1523569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition?p=1523446#post1523446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Like Batman Begins.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not familiar with the example, could you please explain it to me?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T20:15:35-07:00","id":1523588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition?p=1523556#post1523556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (That being said, I <i>do</i> think the Silver Ladder teaches the Lex Magica Merit to others much more readily that the Mysterium would hand out Egregore. It's useful to Sentinels and other Consillium officials, and those are the most likely to have some tie to the Ladder &quot;Look! Participating in the system we set up makes you better at magic! <i>Participate in our system, damn you</i>!&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the other side of it is that I think some of this isn't really predicated on a type of codified knowledge that a person can learn, understand, and then apply as they please in the same way you could service a car engine or something. I think of a lot of it along the lines of the other thing that the Mysterium book said; that you didn't really get to stay in the egregore if you stopped being a member of the Order, because that connection was predicated on a form of attunement based in being immersed in the lifestyle, deeply contemplative and abiding by the mystical philosophy. If you become detached from that (including the extent to which the Mysterium places some of the strongest emphasis on being a communal experience), then you fall out of sync with the egregore.<br /> <br /> Several of the other Order Merits that are equivalent are kind of highly refined forms of yantra, in the context of how there are things like Order specific tool yantras. I read into that as meaning that really feeling how the symbolism of those tools translates into one's imago is not just something you learn, it's something you live through your ideas of what magic is and is for. Other people can recognise the symbolism of symbols of authority at a more superficial level, but you need to really have &quot;Magic is Humanity's Birthright&quot; to make spells out of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T23:29:20-07:00","id":1523606,"title":"","content":"Oh, I 100% believe you need to buy into the Order philosophy to be able to <i>purchase</i> the Merits. Whether that's expressed in-game as someone walking you through the trick of it (Masque and Egregore would probably need a dedicated teacher 90% of the time) or a kind of auto didactic comprehension of the fundamental principles that the Order is working off of (Lex Magica, Techn\u00e9) is more fluid, but otherwise it hinges on the character buying into the core concept, and is expressed mechanically by the Status dot.<br /> <br /> Which also means that straying too far from your dual philosophy will nullify the Merits. You want Egregore <i>and</i> Techn\u00e9? That's a <i>fine</i> line to walk<br /> <br /> (I also prefer it being an option because otherwise that one dot of Status is objectively inferior to just taking Ally dots.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T08:24:55-07:00","id":1523636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition?p=1523606#post1523606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (I also prefer it being an option because otherwise that one dot of Status is objectively inferior to just taking Ally dots.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you becoming a partial member of a second Order because it's the story you want to tell with the character, or for the mechanical benefits?<br /> <br /> I do not believe that there is mechanical parity across the board between <i>any</i> one dot of Merits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T08:44:31-07:00","id":1523638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition?p=1523636#post1523636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you becoming a partial member of a second Order because it's the story you want to tell with the character, or for the mechanical benefits?<br /> <br /> I do not believe that there is mechanical parity across the board between <i>any</i> one dot of Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>There doesn't need to be mechanical parity, but I dont like mechanically pointless rules. In this case, Ally and Status represent largely the same thing (you work very closely with this group, to a degree that they acknowledge you as a firm ally), but one allows you to ask favors while the other... does pretty much the same thing. Status 1 outside of your Order doesn't allow for requisitioning, and you can't effectively use it outside your Consillium due to the increasing penalty abroad. So... what benefit does it give, mechanically or narratively, that Ally doesn't give? And if there <i>isn't</i> a difference, why bother to add the 1-dot caveat at all?<br /> <br /> All of which is a personal nit-pick, obviously, and easy to house-rule if in the unlikely event thag it ever becomes an issue. That dot of Status could give you access to that Order's Yantras, or -as spawned this- allow you to purchase the special Order Merits (Techn\u00e9, Lex Magica, Egregore, Masque, Adamant Hand). Or both. Whatever works for the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T12:43:33-07:00","id":1523729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523395-five-atlanthean-mysteries-and-egregore-in-second-edition?p=1523638#post1523638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There doesn't need to be mechanical parity, but I dont like mechanically pointless rules. In this case, Ally and Status represent largely the same thing (you work very closely with this group, to a degree that they acknowledge you as a firm ally), but one allows you to ask favors while the other... does pretty much the same thing. Status 1 outside of your Order doesn't allow for requisitioning, and you can't effectively use it outside your Consillium due to the increasing penalty abroad. So... what benefit does it give, mechanically or narratively, that Ally doesn't give? And if there <i>isn't</i> a difference, why bother to add the 1-dot caveat at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ally does not innately give itself as a bonus to social rolls against members of the allied group. It forms part of a dice pool to try and get them to do what you'd want if it exceeds certain boundaries, potentially offset by the penalty that the scope of the overstepping entails, and with a potential to have the rating reduced or even nullified. You might get to reassign the dots because of Sanctity of Merits, but you can request your way into losing your Allies altogether.<br /> <br /> On top of the more freeform extent to which the specifics of how the alliance actually works have to be determined by initial collaboration with the Storyteller. Depending on the arrived at conclusion and the actual nature of the Ally, it could reasonably be a bit narrow or specific. <br /> <br /> Status confers an across the board social dice bonus when engaging with people within the organisation who owe the character some deference (which, in the case of Awakened Orders, can include Sleeper and Sleepwalker members, to help for only having the one dot of it), and the procurements available strike me as more of an entitlement to rank. I feel the worst you would tend to get out of looking for more than you're entitled to is denial, as opposed to potentially losing standing in the organization altogether.<br /> <br /> As far as Orders and their magical resources go, I would look at the description of the setting and think that a lot that is proprietary between them comes with high values for the Ally Merit as a matter of course. Being at the lowest rung of an Order only nets you minor things, but at least they're benefits innate to being part of the in group. Being outside of an Order but the bare minimum of friendly with it seems quite plausible as the sort of thing where asking for anything magical at all is constantly jeopardizing that friendship.<br /> <br /> Like, think about what it would mean to be in the Mysterium or Guardians and being an Ally to such, and the consequences of asking for access to something kept in one of their special vaults. I think the mechanics ascribed to each Merit align fairly well with how those scenarios would play out.<br /> <br /> Status not being a strictly superior Merit to Allies by virtue of the fact that it firmly comes with duties to carry out in order to maintain that standing.<br /> <br /> On a related note, looking at the way Order Status is phrased, I'd feel quite reasonable in ruling Order specific Merits as falling under the umbrella of &quot;people who are already in a different Order can't use their one dot of Status for requisitions&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}